// Fixture for Qt.Mechanics.LineLength. Lines are tagged to say whether the rule must
// report them. Run with tests/run-linelength-test.sh.
//
// The rule was previously `extends: existence` with a raw regex. That form
// went through Vale's token pipeline, where any standalone vocabulary term
// silenced the match. The vocabulary cases below are the regression guard.
// silenced the match. The VOCAB cases below are the regression guard.
/*!
    \page linelength-fixture.html
    \title LineLength fixture

    \section1 Plain prose

    EXPECT-CLEAN short line, well under the limit.
    EXPECT-FLAG alpha bravo charlie delta echo foxtrot golf hotel india juliet kilo lima
    EXPECT-CLEAN exactly eighty columns wide, counting every character here ok

    \section1 Vocabulary terms must not suppress the rule

    EXPECT-FLAG \QUL alpha bravo charlie delta echo foxtrot golf hotel india juliet kilo
    EXPECT-FLAG Qul::PlatformInterface::log alpha bravo charlie delta echo foxtrot golf hotel
    EXPECT-FLAG Renesas alpha bravo charlie delta echo foxtrot golf hotel india juliet kilo
    EXPECT-FLAG \li \sup{\l{Qul::PlatformInterface::DrawingEngine}{Hardware accelerated blitting}}

    \section1 Macros and brace commands must not suppress it

    EXPECT-FLAG \supportedWithNote 1 alpha bravo charlie delta echo foxtrot golf hotel india
    EXPECT-FLAG \uicontrol{Apply} alpha bravo charlie delta echo foxtrot golf hotel india ju
    EXPECT-FLAG \tm{PSOC} alpha bravo charlie delta echo foxtrot golf hotel india juliet kil

    \section1 Columns, not bytes

    EXPECT-CLEAN \li \l{Infineon PSOC Edge E84}{Infineon PSOC™ Edge E84 Kit}
    EXPECT-FLAG \li PSOC™ alpha bravo charlie delta echo foxtrot golf hotel india juliet kilo

    \section1 Comment exemption

    EXPECT-CLEAN is the next line: a commented-out long line stays exempt.
//  EXPECT-CLEAN alpha bravo charlie delta echo foxtrot golf hotel india juliet kilo lima mike
*/
